// Title: Potential In-Memory Download And Compile Of Payloads
// Sigma ID: 13db8d2e-7723-4c2c-93c1-a4d36994f7ef
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sohan G (D4rkCiph3r), Red Canary (idea)
// Date: 2023-08-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, execution, T1059.007, T1105
// Description: Detects potential in-memory downloading and compiling of applets using curl and osacompile as
//   seen used by XCSSET malware
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/mac-application-bundles/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_susp_in_memory_download_and_compile.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "osacompile" and ProcessCommandLine contains "curl"
